            <ArticleTitle>[The serum level transformation of interleukin 18 before and after SIT in patients with allergic rhinitis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>210-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To survey the role of IL-18 in the pathogenesis of allergic rhinitis, and to discuss the mechanism of specific immunotherapy (SIT).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">The serum levels of IL-18 in patients with allergic rhinitis and the health control were detected by ELISA before and after SIT (for l year).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULT" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The levels of IL-18 in patients before SIT were (88.33 +/- 35. 95)ng/L, significantly lower than that in healthy control(149 +/- 47.37)ng/L, and the level after SIT (199.22 +/- 58.82 )ng/L was significantly higher than that before SIT. There was no significant difference between the healthy after-SIT.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">IL-18 plays an important role in the pathogenesis of allergic inflammation and the SIT therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
